{%- comment -%}
  ymws-portal-gate.liquid
  Yerba Madre Wholesale ‚Äî tag gate for the Recharge Affinity portal pages

  WHAT IT DOES
    The embedded Recharge Affinity portal renders INSIDE the theme layout (its pages live under
    /tools/recurring/portal/...). This snippet outputs a "not approved" notice ‚Äî and nothing else ‚Äî when the visitor is
    a LOGGED-IN customer who does NOT currently have the Shopify tag `wholesale-approved`. The theme layout then shows
    that notice INSTEAD of the portal content, so the portal's markup and scripts are never sent to that customer.
    This closes every entry point at once (the account-menu "Subscriptions" item, the tag-gated link, a bookmarked URL),
    including the Recharge menu item that Liquid cannot hide.

  HOW IT IS WIRED (3 lines in layout/theme.liquid, around {{ content_for_layout }})
    {%- capture ymws_gate -%}{% render 'ymws-portal-gate' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if ymws_gate contains 'data-ymws-blocked' -%}
      {{ ymws_gate }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    {%- endif -%}

  WHAT IT DECIDES
    - Not on a portal URL                       -> prints nothing (storefront pages are untouched)
    - Logged-in customer WITH wholesale-approved -> prints nothing (portal loads normally)
    - Logged-in customer WITHOUT the tag         -> prints the notice (portal content is suppressed)
    - Guest (no `customer`)                      -> prints nothing. See LIMITATION.
    Live at render time: nothing is cached; remove the tag and the next page load is blocked.

  LIMITATION (important)
    Liquid can only judge a visitor Shopify has logged in. A visitor holding a Recharge email "manage subscription" link
    with a token, but NOT logged in to the storefront, has no `customer`, so this gate cannot tell who they are and lets
    them through (blocking them would also break legitimate approved customers using those email links). Renewals and
    portal edits for such visitors are still protected by the Recharge quantity-guard extension and the server-side
    safety net. This is a display control like the theme's own page gating, not a security boundary.

  Read-only: reads tags, never writes to the customer record.

  Optional parameters:
    {% render 'ymws-portal-gate', portal_path: '/tools/recurring/portal', home_url: '/', message: 'Your account must be approved ...' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ymws_approval_tag = 'wholesale-approved'
  assign ymws_portal_path = portal_path | default: '/tools/recurring/portal'
  assign ymws_home_url = home_url | default: '/'
  assign ymws_notice = message | default: 'Your account must be approved for wholesale to manage subscriptions.'

  assign ymws_is_portal = false
  if request.path contains ymws_portal_path
    assign ymws_is_portal = true
  endif

  # Exact tag name, ignoring letter case and stray spaces (Shopify treats tags case-insensitively).
  assign ymws_approved = false
  if customer
    for ymws_tag in customer.tags
      assign ymws_tag_normalized = ymws_tag | strip | downcase
      if ymws_tag_normalized == ymws_approval_tag
        assign ymws_approved = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # Block ONLY when we positively know the visitor is a logged-in customer who lacks the tag.
  assign ymws_block = false
  if ymws_is_portal and customer and ymws_approved == false
    assign ymws_block = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if ymws_block -%}
  <div id="ymws-portal-blocked" data-ymws-blocked role="alert" style="max-width:640px;margin:64px auto;padding:0 16px;text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:1.125rem;line-height:1.5;">{{ ymws_notice | escape }}</p>
    <p><a href="{{ ymws_home_url | escape }}">Return to the store</a></p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
